cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "NomosGuard: deterministic security reasoning core"
abstract: >-
  NomosGuard keeps the decision boundary away from language models: every
  security conclusion must arrive as a structured claim with a cited
  evidence fragment, recorded in an append-only SHA-256 hash-chained ledger
  with write-ahead recovery. An attack-path rule engine and a fail-closed
  policy gate consume that ledger, so the same evidence always yields the
  same verdict and tampering is detectable.
authors:
  - family-names: "Furox"
    given-names: "Art"
version: 0.7.10
date-released: "2026-10-21"
license: Apache-2.0
repository-code: "https://github.com/Furox-Art/nomosguard"
url: "https://github.com/Furox-Art/nomosguard"
keywords:
  - security
  - evidence ledger
  - hash chain
  - tamper evident
  - policy gate
  - attack graph
  - agent security
  - deterministic reasoning
